      "writtenOn": "2016-08-10T21:58:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Mention LetsEncrypt in the package comment.\n\nAlso, move this up a level already out of internal.\n\nActually I think it could even be in the top-level package: acme.Manager sounds much better than manager.Manager. But I imagine you want to use \"acme\" for the low-level guts once we expose those.\n\nSo, how about package \"autocert\":\n\n   golang.org/x/crypto/acme/autocert\n\nSo then this is:\n\n   // Package autocert provides automatic access to certificates from LetsEncrypt\n   // and any other ACME-based CA.\n\nAnd the type is \"autocert.Manager\".",
      "revId": "e69dcecf0d3565b7e7af7eb3c8fc3cd2e8e53991",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
